## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Minora Finance React application.

### Changes Made

1. **Installed Dependencies**
   - Added `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) to project dependencies
   - Updated package.json with the new dependency
   - Created package-lock.json to lock dependency versions

2. **Integrated Analytics Component**
   - Modified `src/App.tsx`:
     - Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/react`
     - Added `<Analytics />` component at the root level of the app (inside Router but outside the main content div)
   - Followed official Vercel documentation for React integration

### Implementation Details

- **Framework**: React + Vite
- **Integration Method**: Used React-specific import (`@vercel/analytics/react`)
- **Component Placement**: Added Analytics component inside the Router component to ensure it tracks all route changes
- **Documentation Source**: Fetched latest instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

### Verification Steps Completed

✅ Package installation successful (no vulnerabilities)
✅ Build completed successfully (no errors)
✅ Linter passed (no new errors introduced)
✅ All changes preserve existing code structure

### Next Steps for Deployment

To complete the setup:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
3. After deployment, analytics data will automatically be collected and available in the Vercel dashboard

### Files Modified

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - New file with locked dependency versions
- `src/App.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

No existing functionality was affected by these changes.
